Patch 001: return to previous keyboard after inserting

What: adds an opt-in setting, "Return to previous keyboard after inserting" (default off),
next to "Auto-start recording" on the settings screen. When it is on and a dictation has just
been typed into the field (not the clipboard fallback), with nothing recording, nothing left in
the queue and no failed or parked recording waiting for resend, the keyboard hands control back
to the keyboard that opened it: switchToPreviousInputMethod() on API 28+, requestHideSelf(0) if
that fails or on older Android. Errors, parked recordings and cancel never trigger it. With the
setting off the app behaves exactly as upstream. The decision is a pure function
(ReturnToPreviousKeyboard) with a JVM unit test. Also adds a "switch to previous keyboard" key
(bottom row, left of the space bar) that is always available regardless of that setting: it calls
the same switchToPreviousInputMethod()-then-fallback logic, falling back to the input method
picker instead of requestHideSelf(0) since there may be nothing to hand dictation back to.

Why: SPEC.md R6. HeliBoard's mic key opens this keyboard for voice input; without this the user
has to switch back by hand after every dictation.

When to delete: once upstream ships an equivalent setting.

Base: rustemar/voice-keyboard v1.9.1 (02ff1a4bfa626744dfed42b55741f5c55e80060a).
Generated with git diff from a clean checkout of that tag; apply with git apply.

